WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634
-I know you are a great lover of
crime documentaries,

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
crime novels,
real true crime books.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you've had
some interactions,

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
some brushes with danger
recently.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:10.910 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, yes.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.914
I don't -- you know, I don't
want crime to happen to me,

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:15.715 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but I'm a --

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:16.783 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's why
I'm running for mayor.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:20.053 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want crime
to happen to me.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.790 line:92%
I like -- I love true crime

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.126
and have been a little obsessed
with it.

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went on a date once
with a wonderful young lady,

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
who halfway through the date
revealed that her dad

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:34.968
had worked on the Jonbenet case,
and I was just like, "Whoa!"

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:38.905
And then I asked her a thousand
questions about Jonbenet,

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we didn't have
a second date.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.474 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I have always wanted to
solve a crime.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I woke up
a couple months ago.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was on a break
after a lot of touring,

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:52.118
and I went outside my house
in Los Angeles and my car --

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:52.886 size:81% position:41% line:92%
well, my car was shut.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.588
I went inside
and it'd been rummaged through.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
Someone had been in there
and they left a hat.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:02.295
They left a baseball cap
on the passenger side seat.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.130 line:92%
So I went -- I go, "Aha!"

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my car had been
broken into before.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:09.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I go, "This time, we got
a break in the case."

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I go inside
and I got my surgical gloves.

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:15.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I come back out
and I had a Ziploc bag

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:19.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I had my surgical gloves
and I grabbed it just so.

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:21.881 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You know? Not tainted.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:22.849 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.117 line:92%
And I put it in the Ziploc bag.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I remembered that
during the O.J. case,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Dennis Fong,
you know that guy.

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:31.758
He ruined some of the DNA
because it got too warm outside.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:35.862
So I put it in the refrigerator.
So I take the hat and the bag.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:36.396 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "I'm no Dennis Fong."
I put it in the fridge.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.233 line:92%
Then I called the authorities.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:43.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then I waited in front of
my house like this.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:43.770 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Because I was, like,

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.005 size:78% position:39%
"Fellas, don't worry.
It's under control."

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you've pretty much done
all the work for them.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.143 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, absolutely.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:50.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've done the sleuthing
and the forensics already.

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:57.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're safely
in my crisper drawer.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they show up and they go,
"What's the situation?"

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go,
"Someone broke into my car."

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said,
"Did they break a window?"

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "No, I leave
my car unlocked."

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:08.394
Because people used to break in
and break the windows.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
So now I leave it unlocked.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they said,
"What did they take?"

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:15.068 size:84% position:42%
I said, "I have no idea
if they took anything,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I have no idea
what's in my car."

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:20.440
You know, I'll find, like,
my wife's glasses sometimes

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.474 line:92%
and wear them if it's sunny.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:24.177
So I have no -- it's just
a scavenger hunt in there.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:26.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said, "Why haven't you
ever called us before?"

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:30.984
And I said, "Because now we have
a break in the case."

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:31.518 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:34.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I led these two LAPD
officers in my house

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.522 size:75% position:38% line:92%
to the refrigerator.

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I opened it up
and I took out the hat.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:41.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"He left his hat in the car."

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:42.896 size:78% position:39% line:92%
They're like, "Okay."

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:46.566
And I was like, "So you can run
that through CODIS."

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.368 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:52.539
"You can run that and maybe you
can get a hit on who it is."

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:55.008
They were like, "Why would
we run it through CODIS?"

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.844
And I was like,
"Because he committed a crime."

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.245 line:92%
They were like, "Barely."

00:02:59.245 --> 00:02:59.879 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:03.316
They were like,
"One, he didn't break and enter

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:05.418 line:92%
because you left your car open.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.653 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Two, he stole nothing.

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:09.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe we have him
for trespassing.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:12.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we don't do
a national DNA search."

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:16.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You could frame it
as the guy gave you a hat.

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:19.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is an interesting way
to look at it.

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:20.567 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.136 line:92%
Real glass half full type guy.

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:24.270 line:92%
Me, some guy touched my car,

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm gonna nail him
because of the DNA.

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.074 line:92%
But I said to them, you know,

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:30.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, "You know, this can
escalate, you know?

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:33.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
Today it's a car.
Tomorrow, it's an Escalade.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
He escalates."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:36.816 size:78% position:39%
And so -- but I said,
"You know, Manson."

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:39.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't like to
speak ill of the dead,

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.321 line:92%
but he was a lousy guy, right?

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:42.121 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.058
He would creepy crawl around --
that's his term.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-People's houses and stuff.

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:50.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he gradually --
he was up to no good.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:50.597 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:52.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I said, I said,
"I understand that,

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.634 line:92%
but what if this guy escalates?

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:55.802 line:92%
Don't you want his DNA on file?"

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:58.371
And they're like, "What file?
What are you talking about?"

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:02.308
And they're like, "The only way
we would need a DNA profile

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:05.678
is if" -- and then I said,
"If he murders somebody."

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:08.948
Then I remembered that sometimes
serial killers

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
like to help the police,
you know?

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:14.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this whole time I've been
talking about "this guy"

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:15.755 size:75% position:38% line:92%
in the third person.

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:19.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "he's quite cunning,
but he will be back."

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:20.326 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:23.463
And then my friend had had her
car broken into down the street,

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said,
"You should go ask her,

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:26.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
because her car
was also broken into."

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they said, "Was anything
stolen from hers?"

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:31.904
I go, "I don't know. Let me let
her know that you're coming."

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"The police are coming.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:37.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tell them
that he stole something."

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:40.680
Which I thought was a great way
to get the hat, again,

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:44.651
which is nice and cool in the
fridge, in the national system.

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:48.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
It turns out that that is
framing someone for a crime.

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:48.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:52.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I will break rules
to get these guys behind bars.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:52.792 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:53.826 line:92%
-If they're watching right now,

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:56.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
they should know you're
the wrong guy to mess with.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.163 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Absolutely.

00:04:57.163 --> 00:05:03.736
You come in my RAV4 and quickly
realize I have no valuables.

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:04.637 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How dare you.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:08.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the mud on the carpet,
oh, that's mine?

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.877 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
All right.

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:14.580
-I want to say real quick, so
exciting, "Big Mouth" is back.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fantastic show.
-Yes.

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:21.654 size:78% position:39%
Created by Nick Kroll
and Andrew Goldberg.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's based on
their friendship.

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:25.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nick and Andrew and I get to
voice Andrew

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:28.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
alongside my very good friend,
Nick Kroll,

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:31.331
who also voices
the hormone monster seen there.

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.131 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-It's a fantastic show.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:34.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm so excited
it's back for a second season.

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:38.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am so excited, too.
-It's always great to see you.

